{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/484906-a-devotion-like-system-for-changeling","id":484906,"title":"A Devotion-like system for Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-18T15:53:33-07:00","id":484906,"title":"A Devotion-like system for Changeling","content":"I don't know if 2e will have this or not, but I think a system that allows for modifications and additions to Contracts would be a great addition. The five dot system is a bit too limiting- it's basically saying you can only interact with these broad concepts in one of five ways. Vampire brilliantly solved this problem with Devotions, and I've always thought the other games (Changeling and Geist) that used the &quot;five dot powers&quot; system desperately needed something like them. <br /> <br /> For a name, how about Clauses? Since they represent alterations to Contracts made with concepts. What kinds of effects would be reasonable for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T15:58:16-07:00","id":484929,"title":"","content":"I think in 2nd edition Changeling contracts will all be individualized and not have a 1-5 scale. So, there may be a 3 dot contract that's only that level 3 power, for instance. So, for 2nd edition it'd be pretty easy to just make a new one, I imagine.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about doing it for 1st edition in the mean time, I'd suggest doing a redo of Goblin Vow. Instead of taking goblin vow for a concept, take it for a contract, and in exchange for some 'favor' you do, you can alter the base effect one time. Then, if you pay some experience surcharge after using it a few times, you can call upon that same effect without as high a price later? Call them 'Goblin Clauses&quot; or something. (To note, a clause is already an individual contract level in 1st edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T16:42:46-07:00","id":484942,"title":"","content":"Goblin Contracts sort of do that. I mean you buy them in individual clauses.<br /> <br /> Geist has Ceremonies with individual nonrelated powers. Keys and Manifestations are deeply themed and harder to divorce from that system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Mo